 "ownerDecisions": [
  "Q-HE3A-1 = (c) (2026-10-13, owner via the lane monitor, verbatim as architecture/host-interface-amendment-hs43/amendment.json records it): (c) readlink exe for the I07 writer",
  "Q-HE3A-1b = (a) (2026-10-13, owner via the lane monitor, verbatim as architecture/host-interface-amendment-hs43/amendment.json records it): (a) HE-003A merges first; the readlink exe check is decided-but-open, landing after the chain: seccomp v3 readlinkat duty for EFFECT_GATE (parallel lane, with/after the slot-234 §4.3 amendment) → republished programs + edge record v3 (primary) → R10 re-vendor + check. HE-007 obligations: writer uid/gid 0, dumpable, empty permitted set.",
  "Q-HE3D-3 = (a) (2026-10-15, the lane monitor under the owner's delegation, HE-003D decisions, verbatim): the writer exe check isn't in HE-003D. It goes in HE-003A2 after the seccomp and programs chain merges; the enrolled path comes from the configuration (G4).",
  "Q-PR-1..10 = (a) (2026-10-15, the lane monitor under the owner's delegation, PROGRAMS-REPUBLISH decisions, verbatim): [lane monitor] PROGRAMS-REPUBLISH: Q-PR-1..10 = (a), all of them. Monitor (owner-delegated), 2026-10-15; record verbatim.\n- a new architecture/compiled-filter-programs-v2/;\n- only EFFECT_GATE re-emitted, with the other 12 proven equal to 232's bytes;\n- edge record v3 = v2's 31 rows plus 2;\n- the R10 consumer path contracts/seccomp-v4/;\n- the other rows unchanged;\n- the pinned v4 model plus the exact 6-instruction-block layer check;\n- v4 vector replay;\n- a status.json adoption discharging v4's obligation;\n- no riders;\n- MET-ENFORCE-029, with the contract reviewed on 9f251d5 and rebased unchanged onto 239's merge at mechanics time.\nGo ahead with the contract design and the independent review, as light work."
 ],
 "notes": [
  "v2's 31 artefacts are carried unchanged and in order, statuses included: v2's two EFFECT_GATE rows (consumer HE-002S) were REGISTERED_BEFORE_USE when v2 was published; HE-002S has since merged in R10, so they are IN_USE there, and they are kept as recorded.",
  "The twelve programs of the other six roles are also seccomp allowlists v4's programs: v4's filterDigests and programLengths for those roles equal v3's, and the bytes at their v2 provider paths are unchanged, so their v2 rows stay as they are. SERVER's two programs stay PUBLISHED_UNREGISTERED.",
  "The two new rows register v4's EFFECT_GATE programs, published by MET-ENFORCE-029 in architecture/compiled-filter-programs-v2/programs/, for R10's HE-003A2 (the packet Q-HE3D-3 (a) names for the writer executable check) under host-enforcement/contracts/seccomp-v4/. Whether R10 keeps contracts/seccomp-v3/EFFECT_GATE.* is R10's decision.",
  "A program row with providerCommit null is published by its providerPacket; its commit is that packet's merge commit.",
  "The programs are data (the v4 contract's compiled filters), not implementation source, so the boundary rule holds."
 ]
}
